# Local secrets for development.
#
# Copy this file to  application-local-secret.properties  in the same folder
# (beside pom.xml), fill in JWT_SECRET, and the application reads it on
# every run — from IntelliJ, from mvnw, from anywhere — with nothing to set in a
# run configuration.
#
# The real file is already in .gitignore and must never be committed.
#
# These are properties-file keys, so there is no ";" separator to get wrong.
# A real JWT_SECRET environment variable takes precedence over this file.
#
# Environment variables still work and still win over this file, which is how
# deployment supplies them. This file is only a convenience for a workstation.

# Signs access tokens, and encrypts queued email payloads by default.
# Any random string of 32 characters or more. Change it for anything real.
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-your-own-random-string-of-32-characters-or-more

# The default local profile uses mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017 and jachai_local.
# No Atlas credentials belong in this workstation file. For production, set
# MONGODB_URI and optionally MONGODB_DATABASE in the deployment environment.

# Uncomment when you have the credentials. Each is optional; the application
# starts without them and reports the feature as unavailable.
# app.auth.google.client-id=
# spring.ai.google.genai.api-key=
